- **Direct Bank Payouts:** The moment a corporate trip is marked completed and digital trip telemetry is verified, the net earnings are dispatched directly to the driver's linked bank account (IMPS/UPI).
- **Transparent Trip Breakdown:** Drivers see the exact breakdown of distance, trip parameters, and incentives before accepting any trip.
- **Century Milestone Bonus:** To reward dedication, every commercial driver who onboards and activates on the AdhocX platform unlocks performance cash bonuses directly to their registered bank account.

\`\`\`
[Trip Completion Verified] 
       │
       ▼
[Automated Ledger Entry Generated]
       │
       ▼
[Instant IMPS / UPI Bank Dispatch] ──> Under 60 Minutes Guaranteed
\`\`\`

---

## Standardized Terms & Guaranteed Payouts

Unlike consumer rideshare apps that leave drivers stranded in distant industrial or suburban clusters with uncertain fares, AdhocX provides:
1. **Clear Outstation Parameters:** Guaranteed confirmed routes with zero hidden deductions.
2. **Dedicated Bulk Contract Matching:** Continuous morning and evening shift assignments for predictable monthly revenue.
3. **24/7 Driver Support & Dispute Protection:** Dedicated hotline for route discrepancies, toll claims, and parking reimbursements.
        `
      },
      'bulk-fleet-outsourcing-vs-spot-dispatch-guide': {
        title: 'Bulk Fleet Outsourcing vs Spot Dispatch: A Strategic Guide for Corporate Logistics',
        slug: 'bulk-fleet-outsourcing-vs-spot-dispatch-guide',
        excerpt: 'Comparing dedicated monthly fleet retainers against dynamic on-demand spot dispatching to optimize corporate transport budgets and maintain guaranteed SLA punctuality.',
        category: 'Enterprise Logistics',
        tags: ['Fleet Optimization', 'B2B Logistics', 'Cost Reduction'],
        coverImage: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586528116311-ad8dd3c8310d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
        authorName: 'AdhocX Enterprise Solutions',
        authorRole: 'Supply Chain Strategy Director',
        readTime: '6 min read',
        views: 289,
        publishedAt: '2026-09-08T08:15:00Z',
        seoKeywords: 'corporate fleet outsourcing, employee transit strategy, B2B cab spot dispatch',
        content: `
## The Strategic Dilemma: Fixed Retainer or On-Demand Flexibility?

Corporate facilities and logistics executives frequently debate the most cost-effective fleet structure:
- Should the company lease a dedicated fleet of 50 vehicles on fixed monthly retainer?
- Or should the enterprise operate a lean core fleet and fulfill peak fluctuations through digital spot marketplaces?

---

## Comparative Breakdown: Dedicated vs. Spot Dispatch

| Operational Metric | Dedicated Fleet Retainer | AdhocX Dynamic Spot Fulfillment |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Fixed Monthly Cost** | High (fixed vehicle rent + driver minimums) | **Zero (pay-per-trip basis)** |
| **Idle Vehicle Waste** | Significant on weekends/holidays (Substantial idle loss) | **Zero idle fleet liability** |
| **Peak Surge Scalability** | Rigid (limited to contracted vehicles) | **Infinite elasticity across verified pool** |
| **Driver Backup Redundancy** | Vulnerable to driver absenteeism | **Automated fallback assignment in < 5 mins** |
| **Billing Transparency** | Paper log sheets & manual invoice audits | **Digital GPS telemetry & automated invoices** |

---

## The Optimal Hybrid Architecture: The 70/30 Rule

Top-performing enterprises adopt a **hybrid mobility strategy**:
1. **Core Retainer Baseline:** Maintain dedicated contracts for predictable, high-volume recurring employee routes.
2. **Elastic On-Demand Buffer with AdhocX:** Utilize AdhocX's automated bidding and dispatch marketplace for emergency shifts, client airport transfers, VIP delegations, and seasonal peaks.
        `
      }
    };

    function parseMarkdownToHTML(md) {
      if (!md) return '';
      let html = md.trim();

      html = html.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');

      html = html.replace(/```([\s\S]*?)```/g, (match, code) => {
        return `<pre class="article-code-block"><code>${code.trim()}</code></pre>`;
      });

      html = html.replace(/(\|.+?\|\n\|[-:| ]+\|\n(?:\|.+?\|\n?)+)/g, (match) => {
        const rows = match.trim().split('\n');
        const headers = rows[0].split('|').filter(c => c.trim()).map(c => `<th>${c.trim()}</th>`).join('');
        const bodyRows = rows.slice(2).map(r => {
          const cells = r.split('|').filter(c => c.trim()).map(c => `<td>${c.trim().replace(/\*\*(.*?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>')}</td>`).join('');
          return `<tr>${cells}</tr>`;
        }).join('');
        return `<div class="table-responsive"><table class="article-data-table"><thead><tr>${headers}</tr></thead><tbody>${bodyRows}</tbody></table></div>`;
      });

      let headingIndex = 0;
      html = html.replace(/^### (.*$)/gim, (m, text) => {
        headingIndex++;
        const id = `section-${headingIndex}`;
        return `<h3 id="${id}" class="article-heading-h3">${text.trim()}</h3>`;
      });

      html = html.replace(/^## (.*$)/gim, (m, text) => {
        headingIndex++;
        const id = `section-${headingIndex}`;
        return `<h2 id="${id}" class="article-heading-h2">${text.trim()}</h2>`;
      });

      html = html.replace(/\*\*(.*?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>');
      html = html.replace(/\*(.*?)\*/g, '<em>$1</em>');
      html = html.replace(/^> (.*$)/gim, '<blockquote class="article-quote"><p>$1</p></blockquote>');
      html = html.replace(/^---$/gim, '<hr class="article-divider" />');
      html = html.replace(/^\- (.*$)/gim, '<li class="article-list-item">$1</li>');
      html = html.replace(/((?:<li class="article-list-item">.*<\/li>\n?)+)/g, '<ul class="article-ul">$1</ul>');
      html = html.replace(/^\d+\. (.*$)/gim, '<li class="article-ol-item">$1</li>');
      html = html.replace(/((?:<li class="article-ol-item">.*<\/li>\n?)+)/g, '<ol class="article-ol">$1</ol>');

      const blocks = html.split(/\n\n+/);
      html = blocks.map(block => {
        block = block.trim();
        if (
          block.startsWith('<h') ||
          block.startsWith('<pre') ||
          block.startsWith('<div') ||
          block.startsWith('<blockquote') ||
          block.startsWith('<ul') ||
          block.startsWith('<ol') ||
          block.startsWith('<hr')
        ) {
          return block;
        }
        return `<p class="article-p">${block.replace(/\n/g, '<br/>')}</p>`;
      }).join('\n\n');

      return html;
    }

    function buildTableOfContents() {
      const contentEl = document.getElementById('art-content');
      const tocEl = document.getElementById('toc-nav');
      if (!contentEl || !tocEl) return;

      const headings = contentEl.querySelectorAll('h2, h3');
      if (headings.length === 0) {
        tocEl.innerHTML = '<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:12px;">No sub-sections</span>';
        return;
      }

      tocEl.innerHTML = Array.from(headings).map(h => {
        const isH3 = h.tagName.toLowerCase() === 'h3';
        return `
          <a href="#${h.id}" class="toc-link ${isH3 ? 'toc-sublink' : ''}">
            ${h.textContent}
          </a>
        `;
      }).join('');

      tocEl.querySelectorAll('a').forEach(a => {
        a.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
          e.preventDefault();
          const target = document.querySelector(a.getAttribute('href'));
          if (target) {
            target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
          }
        });
      });
    }

    function renderArticle(art) {
      document.title = `${art.seoTitle || art.title} — AdhocX Insights`;

      document.getElementById('bc-category').textContent = art.category;
      document.getElementById('art-category').textContent = art.category;
      document.getElementById('art-readtime').textContent = `${art.readTime || '5 min read'}`;
      document.getElementById('art-views').textContent = `${(art.views || 0) + 1} Reads`;
      document.getElementById('art-title').textContent = art.title;
      document.getElementById('art-excerpt').textContent = art.excerpt;
      document.getElementById('art-author').textContent = art.authorName || 'AdhocX Team';
      document.getElementById('art-role').textContent = art.authorRole || 'Mobility Operations Research';

      const initials = (art.authorName || 'AX').split(' ').map(n => n[0]).slice(0, 2).join('');
      document.getElementById('art-author-initials').textContent = initials;
      document.getElementById('bio-name').textContent = art.authorName || 'AdhocX Team';

      if (art.publishedAt) {
        const d = new Date(art.publishedAt);
        document.getElementById('art-date').textContent = d.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' });
      }

      if (art.coverImage) {
        document.getElementById('art-cover').src = art.coverImage;
      }

      document.getElementById('art-content').innerHTML = parseMarkdownToHTML(art.content);
      buildTableOfContents();

      const tagsList = document.getElementById('art-tags-list');
      if (art.tags && art.tags.length > 0) {
        tagsList.innerHTML = art.tags.map(t => `<a href="/blogs?search=${encodeURIComponent(t)}" class="tag-pill">#${t}</a>`).join('');
      } else {
        tagsList.innerHTML = `<span class="tag-pill">#${art.category}</span>`;
      }

      const pageUrl = window.location.href;
      const shareTitle = encodeURIComponent(art.title);
      document.getElementById('share-linkedin').onclick = () => window.open(`https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=${encodeURIComponent(pageUrl)}`, '_blank');
      document.getElementById('share-twitter').onclick = () => window.open(`https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=${shareTitle}&url=${encodeURIComponent(pageUrl)}`, '_blank');
      document.getElementById('share-whatsapp').onclick = () => window.open(`https://api.whatsapp.com/send?text=${shareTitle}%20${encodeURIComponent(pageUrl)}`, '_blank');
      document.getElementById('share-copy').onclick = () => {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(pageUrl).then(() => {
          const feedback = document.getElementById('copy-feedback');
          feedback.style.display = 'block';
          setTimeout(() => feedback.style.display = 'none', 3000);
        });
      };

      renderRelatedArticles(art.slug);
    }

    function renderRelatedArticles(currentSlug) {
      const relContainer = document.getElementById('related-grid');
      const allValues = Object.values(SEED_ARTICLES).filter(x => x.slug !== currentSlug);
      relContainer.innerHTML = allValues.slice(0, 2).map(b => `
        <article class="card" style="padding: var(--space-6);">
          <div style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            <span>${b.category}</span> • <span>${b.readTime}</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="h4-title" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
            <a href="/blog-detail?slug=${encodeURIComponent(b.slug)}" style="color: var(--color-text-primary); text-decoration: none;">${b.title}</a>
          </h4>
          <p class="body-text" style="font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 16px;">${b.excerpt}</p>
          <a href="/blog-detail?slug=${encodeURIComponent(b.slug)}" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size: 13px;">Read Article →</a>
        </article>
      `).join('');
    }

    async function initArticle() {
      const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
      const slug = urlParams.get('slug') || 'how-reverse-auction-cuts-enterprise-cab-costs';

      if (SEED_ARTICLES[slug]) {
        renderArticle(SEED_ARTICLES[slug]);
      }

      try {
        const res = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/blogs/${encodeURIComponent(slug)}`);
        if (res.ok) {
          const liveBlog = await res.json();
          if (liveBlog) {
            renderArticle(liveBlog);
          }
        }
      } catch (err) {
        console.log('Serving offline seed article content:', err);
      }
    }

    initArticle();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
